 "findings": [
  "P. nireus preset: extracted emission peaks at 503.0 nm (cited ~505 nm); under UV-A the scale glows #00de7d.",
  "The 3-layer DBR raises the top escape factor at 505 nm from 0.500 to 0.528 (model).",
  "Realizable phoneme films (n 1-2.5) only reshape extraction mildly: escape factor over 450-650 nm ranges 0.31-0.51 across all 43 items, so under blacklight every phoneme glows nearly the same green; in daylight the dye adds 11-79% of Y on top of the film's own reflection.",
  "With the unphysical 'ideal' indices (up to n~200) the films do filter the emission strongly (escape factor down to ~0.1) and blacklight colours diverge - reported only as ideal_unphysical."
 ],
 "citations": [
  "Vukusic P. & Hooper I. (2005) Directionally controlled fluorescence emission in butterflies. Science 310:1151. doi:10.1126/science.1116612",
  "Van Hooijdonk E., Vandenbem C., Berthier S. & Vigneron J.P. (2012) Bi-functional photonic structure in the Papilio nireus (Papilionidae): modeling by scattering-matrix optical simulations. Opt. Express 20:22001. doi:10.1364/OE.20.022001 (peak excitation ~420 nm, peak emission ~505 nm, band 450-650 nm; 2-D PC 1300 nm thick, air cylinders 240 nm diameter / 340 nm hexagonal spacing; lamina gap 1500 nm; DBR 75/35/75 nm)",
  "Wilts B.D., Matsushita A., Arikawa K. & Stavenga D.G. (2015) Spectrally tuned structural and pigmentary coloration of birdwing butterfly wing scales. J. R. Soc. Interface 12:20150717. doi:10.1098/rsif.2015.0717 (fluorescent papiliochromes in Ornithoptera/Troides scales; violet- and UV-absorbing pigments)",
  "CIE 1931 2deg observer and D65 via the colour-science package (as core.colour)."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "Spectral shapes are Gaussian fits to cited peaks and band edges, not digitised spectra.",
  "Quantum yield 0.3 and dye extinction k_max 0.02 are ILLUSTRATIVE (no literature value found).",
  "Extraction is Purcell-free: eta = P_top/(P_top+P_bottom) for in-plane dipole sheets, s/p averaged; vertical dipoles, re-absorption of emission and the 2-D PC's in-plane band gap are ignored.",
  "Reflection is specular, fluorescence is spread over angles; fluor_fraction is indicative only.",
  "Display hexes are exposure-normalised, so a dim blacklight scene shows its hue at display brightness.",
  "Phoneme films use the project pipeline's media (incident medium = film n[0], not necessarily air)."
 ]
}